course: dictionary
lesson: 1265
title: Bury: under the ground, or out of sight
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Squirrels bury nuts in many separate spots for winter.» The squirrel does not leave the nuts lying around. It puts them in holes in the ground and covers them with earth, so bury means to put something under the earth and hide it.
explain: «In AD 79 the volcano Vesuvius buried the town of Pompeii in ash.» Nobody dug a hole for the town. The ash covered it completely and hid it for a very long time. Check the meaning: swap in covered and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Bury can also mean to give all your attention to something. «She buried herself in her book all afternoon.» She did not dig anything. Her mind went deep into the story, so buried yourself means you were completely absorbed in it.
fact: «Bury» means to put something in a hole in the ground and cover it with earth.
fact: «Bury» can mean to put a dead person or animal in the ground, often with a ceremony, to say goodbye.
fact: «Bury» can mean to hide something under other things, as in pirates who bury treasure in stories.
fact: «Buried in» means covered by something, or very busy with it, as in «buried in homework».
fact: The forms are bury, buries, buried and burying: «Yesterday they buried the seeds» and «Today they are burying the seeds».
exercise: «Grey squirrels bury nuts in many separate spots.» What does bury mean here? | Sing loudly to the birds | Throw far out to sea | Wash in a river | * Put in a hole in the ground and cover with earth
exercise: «In AD 79 the volcano Vesuvius buried the town of Pompeii in ash.» What covered the town? | Water | * Ash | Sand from the beach | Snow
exercise: «She buried herself in her book all afternoon.» What does buried yourself in mean? | Hid from her friends under a blanket | * Gave it all her attention | Dug a hole in the garden | Fell asleep on the sofa
test: «They buried their old dog under the apple tree and said a few kind words.» What does buried mean here? | * Put the body in the ground with a goodbye ceremony | Hid it in a cupboard | Painted it bright blue | Gave it a bath
test: «The pirate buried the gold coins on the island.» What does buried mean? | Spent them quickly in town | Cleaned them in the sea | * Hid them under the earth to keep them safe | Counted them slowly
exam: Archaeologists dig up «Roman coins buried long ago». What does buried mean? | * Put in the ground and hidden for a long time | Bought in a shop | Polished until they shine | Thrown into a river
